      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "The lymphotoxin-alpha (LT-alpha) gene is located on chromosome 6 (6p21.1-6p21.3) and it may regulate tumor necrosis factor (TNF) production. TNF is a potent cytokine in the airway inflammatory response. Polymorphisms of TNF-associated genes have been related to asthma. This study investigated an LT-alpha-Ncol polymorphism in the first intron of the LT-alpha gene (LT-alpha-Ncol*1 allele, as a variant type; and LT-alpha-Ncol*2 allele), which may predispose individuals to asthma and atopy."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Polymerase chain reaction-based assays were performed to determine LT-alpha-Ncol genotypes among our subjects. A genetic case control analysis was then performed on 114 atopic asthmatic and 155 non-asthmatic unrelated children."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "There was a statistically higher frequency of LT-alpha-Ncol*1 allele carriers (1/1+1/2) in the subjects with atopic asthma than in controls (OR=1.923; 95% CI = 1.061-3.484; p = 0.031)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The results indicate that LT-alpha-Ncol*1 may be a risk factor for atopic asthma in Taiwanese children."
        }
      ]},
